-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  suite_cli_help_option.adam - `adam check -h` (no banner, no file needed):
  check's help, its options column as wide as check's own widest option
  (build's -o does not belong to it), exit 0
*******************************************************************************/

/*
@@test
  kind cli
  args "--no-banner" "check" "-h"
  exitcode 0
  | USAGE:
  |   adam check <file> [options]
  |
  | Check the program whose main module is <file>: the front end only, nothing built
  |
  | OPTIONS:
  |   -t, --target <target>  The target, by its name or its triple (TARGETS lists them); wins over the main module's @target
  |   --no-banner            Print no banner: for scripts and tests
  |   -h, --help             Show the help of the command given (else adam's)
  |
  | TARGETS:
  |   win64                  x86_64-windows-gnu (default)
  |
  | EXAMPLES:
  |   adam check hello.adam
@@end
*/

module exe suite_cli_help_option;

begin
end.
